--[[c1]] -- Team Shell / Mission 1 -- Code Art plugin shell (owner: Michelangelo).
--[[c2]] -- Runs as the plugin's Script. Child ModuleScripts: Fitter, Lexer (Leonardo),
--[[c3]] -- ImageSource (Donatello, src/image), Equiv + EquivLexer (Raphael), Backup (this folder).
--[[c4]] -- Every write must pass BOTH Fitter.verify (inside transform) and Equiv.check.
--[[c5]] -- Flow: select a script -> enter asset ID -> Preview (exact size from Fitter.predict)
--[[c6]] -- -> Confirm writes via ScriptEditorService:UpdateSourceAsync after Fitter's self-check.
--[[c7]] -- Undo: Studio's undo ignores script Source edits, so every write is preceded by a
--[[c8]] -- persistent backup and a Revert button restores it byte for byte.
--[[c9]] -- Raphael's independent checker (separate lexer)
--[[c10]] -- plugin setting: true once the first-run help has been shown
--[[c11]] -- built-in Studio texture; rbxassetid://0 left the button invisible
--[[c12]] -- UI ----------------------------------------------------------------------
--[[c13]] -- ScrollingFrame so the help section and status fit in a short dock widget.
--[[c14]] -- Hover hints: GuiObjects have no tooltip property, so one shared hint line at the
--[[c15]] -- bottom of the panel shows the text for whatever the mouse is over.
--[[c16]] -- created last (bottom of the panel); tip() only touches it from events
--[[c17]] -- Header + first-run help ---------------------------------------------------
--[[c18]] -- Expanded on first run only. If the setting can't be read, start collapsed (toggle still works).
--[[c19]] -- One-of-N button row. Returns a getter for the current choice.
--[[c20]] -- not via add(): Frame has no Font/Text properties
--[[c21]] -- Filler character (Leonardo: "#" default; only glyphs verified in Studio's editor)
--[[c22]] -- Detail slider (Richard): 5 stops, 0 = Silhouette ... 100 = Features. Default 0, remembered
--[[c23]] -- in plugin setting CodeArt_Level. getLevel() returns 0|25|50|75|100; onLevelChanged(fn) runs
--[[c24]] -- fn(level) when the slider settles (tick click or drag release), not while dragging.
--[[c25]] -- not via add(): Frame has no Font/Text properties
--[[c26]] -- between the end labels; ticks sit at 0, 1/4 ... 1 of its width
--[[c27]] -- One transparent button over the whole track takes all mouse input: a click anywhere snaps to
--[[c28]] -- the nearest tick, and a press-drag-release moves the handle stop by stop.
--[[c29]] -- what the slider displays (differs from `level` only mid-drag)
--[[c30]] -- Listen on the track and on the panel, so a drag that wanders off the track still tracks and ends.
--[[c31]] -- released outside the widget: settle where shown
--[[c32]] -- room for the size line, Features note and image warnings
--[[c33]] -- State -------------------------------------------------------------------
--[[c34]] -- ImageSource adapter ------------------------------------------------------
--[[c35]] -- The ONLY code that knows ImageSource's detail API (Donatello). Slider level 0..100 maps to
--[[c36]] -- detail d = level/100 in [0, 1]. New module: load(id, {detail = d}), img:withDetail(d) re-derives
--[[c37]] -- from cached pixels (no reload), ImageSource.minColumns(d) gives the width floor. Old module
--[[c38]] -- (no minColumns): only the named modes exist, so 0 -> "silhouette", 100 -> "features".
--[[c39]] -- Minimum art width for a level, or nil for no floor beyond the usual 8.
--[[c40]] -- minColumns returns 0 at d = 0 (Silhouette): 0 and nil both mean "no floor".
--[[c41]] -- Fallback (old module or minColumns error): FEATURES_MIN_COLS for any level > 0, i.e. any level
--[[c42]] -- that keeps the mid-tone band. Conservative; pending Leonardo's/Raphael's confirmation.
--[[c43]] -- Preview (criterion 1) -----------------------------------------------------
--[[c44]] -- Loads (or, with reuse, re-derives) the image at `level`, predicts the size and sets `pending`.
--[[c45]] -- ImageSource messages are complete sentences; show verbatim
--[[c46]] -- Mid-tone detail needs >= minCols for eyes/mouth to survive (Raphael's facehole
--[[c47]] -- test: real decal fails at 24, passes from 32). Widen unless the code then won't fit.
--[[c48]] -- Image-quality warnings from ImageSource (low contrast, small ink, ...), shown verbatim.
--[[c49]] -- slider moved while this ran: don't arm Confirm with an old level
--[[c50]] -- ID validation is ImageSource's job (one parser for the whole plugin); show its message verbatim.
--[[c51]] -- Explicit Preview: drop the module's pixel cache so a re-uploaded asset isn't stale.
--[[c52]] -- (Slider settles re-derive with img:withDetail instead and never come through here.)
--[[c53]] -- Slider settled: a shown preview is now stale. Re-derive from cached pixels when the module
--[[c54]] -- supports it (same script and ID); otherwise ask for a fresh Preview. Either way the old
--[[c55]] -- pending job is dropped first, so Confirm can never use the previous level.
